# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# karis-ky Escrow — Staging Environment Configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Loaded by `scripts/deploy.sh --env .env.staging` and
# `scripts/verify_deployment.sh`.
#
# Staging mirrors mainnet topology and parameters so that any deployment-time
# issue surfaces here first. Differences from mainnet are kept minimal:
#   - Different RPC URL (internal staging RPC)
#   - Different network passphrase
#   - Different funding-token contract address (staging-token, not mainnet)
#   - Same admin role but a separate key
#
# Secrets below are **placeholders**. In a real deployment, source these from
# a secret manager (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, etc.) and never commit real
# secrets to the repository.
#
# Schema version: 7 (must match `pub const SCHEMA_VERSION` in escrow/src/lib.rs)
# Interface version: 2
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Network identity
STELLAR_NETWORK=staging
SOROBAN_RPC_URL=https://soroban-staging.internal.example.com
NETWORK_PASSPHRASE="Staging Network ; March 2026"

# WASM build target / artifact (used by deploy.sh + verify_deployment.sh)
WASM_TARGET=wasm32v1-none
WASM_PATH=target/${WASM_TARGET}/release/karis_ky_escrow.wasm

# Deployer identity (REPLACE before use — these are placeholders)
SOURCE_SECRET=SXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
DEPLOYER_ADDRESS=GXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# Expected init parameters — verify_deployment.sh cross-checks the on-chain
# state against these after deployment. Leave blank to skip that check.
EXPECTED_ADMIN=
EXPECTED_INVOICE_ID=
EXPECTED_FUNDING_TOKEN=
EXPECTED_SCHEMA_VERSION=7